  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Parsons Government Services obligated $634M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Parsons Government Services won 136 awards so far, with an average award size of $4.7M. Obligations fell 43.9% year over year. Parsons Government Services received larger obligations from the Department of Defense and the General Services Administration. The Department of Defense obligated $300M for Parsons Government Services, and the General Services Administration obligated $257M. Parsons Government Services also has meaningful obligations in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $289M and in Engineering Services at $212M. Parsons Government Services recorded $69.8M in Computer Systems Design Services and $39.3M in Other Scientific and Technical Consulting Services. Parsons Government Services has smaller obligations across several other NAICS markets, including Custom Computer Programming Services at $11.7M and Professional and Management Development Training at $751K. Fiscal-year comparisons show prior annual obligations of $1.1B in FY21, $1.1B in FY22, $1B in FY23, $1.3B in FY24, and $1.1B in FY25.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Parsons Government Services' biggest buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $300M to Parsons Government Services in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration follows with $257M in obligations. The Department of Energy, Department of Labor, and Department of Transportation also bought work, obligating $38.8M, $24.4M, and $5.6M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets drive Parsons Government Services' federal work?",
        "body": "Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the top market at $289M. Engineering Services is the second-largest market at $212M. Computer Systems Design Services and Other Scientific and Technical Consulting Services add $69.8M and $39.3M respectively, with additional activity in Custom Computer Programming Services at $11.7M and other smaller NAICS markets."
      }
    ]
  },
